cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "seedaudit: auditing a repository's own reproducibility claims with stated detection power"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/seedaudit"
abstract: >-
  seedaudit audits a repository's committed reproducibility claims. It finds
  committed numbers that move when only the random seed changes, scripts that
  claim determinism and are not deterministic, and checks whose own execution
  can create the condition they test. Every verdict carries the closed-form
  detection power of the sampling that produced it, so a clean audit reports a
  quantified upper bound on the intermittency rate that could have escaped
  rather than an implied zero. Research-grade; not flight-qualified, not
  certified and not approved for operational aerospace use.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - determinism
  - detection power
  - intermittent failure
  - flaky tests
  - static analysis
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
